WEBVTT

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:02.590
This girl is Kouyama Mitsuki.

00:00:02.590 --> 00:00:04.100
She's twelve and dreams of becoming a singer.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.780
But unfortunately...

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:07.440
...she only has one year left to live.

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:11.690
We, the Shinigami were asked to keep an 
eye on her until the inevitable fate, but...{Completely changed the line, they didn't go to Mitsuki to TELL her, rather they were TOLD to watch over her until she meets her fate in a year time.}

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:14.340
Today, she's become an adult...

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.450
...and she performed incredibly in the audition.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:17.190
Aren't we...

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:19.310
...changing her destiny?!

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:21.170
Well then...

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:23.030
I wonder what's going to happen today.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:28.670
Do you understand?

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:29.670
Yes.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.300
This is all your fault, Takuto!

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:10.880
Didn't that girl pass the audition?!

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.170
Man.. I was surprised too.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:14.980
I didn't think she would actually be chosen.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:17.190
Don't talk like that about other people's lives!

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:21.170
You're shouting, Meroko.

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:24.860
It couldn't be that you've forgotten
what our job here is?

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:27.100
To make sure that when her one year is up...

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:29.090
...she won't refuse to come with us, right?

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:30.090
Exactly!

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:31.740
So then, it doesn't matter...

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:34.870
...whether or not she passed the audition.

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:36.790
Ah, I see...

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:37.920
...not!

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:40.630
She was willing to return to the house with us...

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:43.710
Now that she's become a singer... it'll be 
 troublesome to have to follow her around.

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:46.630
You let a human like her know the truth...

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:48.340
...and even turned her into a sixteen-year old!

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:50.510
I won't forgive you for a stunt like this!

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:55.960
What's so funny?

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:59.310
You two seem to be so close.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:02:59.880
Huh?

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:03.980
Well, after all...

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:05.280
We are...

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:06.530
...the ones who silence the tears of children.

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:07.950
The Shinigami Duo...

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:09.680
...Spring Onion Ramen!

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:15.290
I'm really grateful for everything.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:16.410
Huh? Oh... It was nothing.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:17.580
By the way...

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:19.880
...that song you sang at the audition...

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.750
...what song was that?

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:23.670
That was...

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:26.480
...the song my father, a musician, wrote.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:28.220
Really...

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.430
Is something wrong?

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:36.270
For some reason, I can't seem to remember 
whether or not I've heard it before...

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:37.890
Hold it!

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:41.190
Don't think that just because you passed 
the audition, you've become an adult!

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:43.960
W-When I'm in this body, I'm all grown up!

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:46.230
Hmm... so then...

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:47.900
Stop harassing her!

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:49.660
Oh... but...

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:52.930
...I can't go home like this, so...

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:54.810
Huh? Oh. Of course.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:09.010
Amazing...

00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:10.130
...I turned back to normal.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.550
Yep. Your chest returned to normal, too.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:14.750
Geez... you're so stingy.

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:15.600
Hey...

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:16.370
Eh?

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:17.480
Do you...

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:19.390
...really plan on becoming a singer?

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:20.040
Yeah.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:21.670
I promised, after all.

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:22.560
Promised?

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:25.570
My promise... with Eichi-kun.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:27.510
Eichi-kun?

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:28.610
Wait, who is that?!

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:29.570
Your sweetheart?

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:30.490
What the hell?!

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:32.740
H-He's not my sweetheart...

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:34.160
...yet.

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:35.950
So that means...

00:04:35.950 --> 00:04:37.490
...he's the one you're longing for?

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:41.420
I...

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:42.750
...two years ago...

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:44.540
...entered a treatment center for the ill.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:46.630
While Grandma was traveling abroad...

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:48.380
...I stayed there with Eichi-kun.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:52.930
He told me his feelings, but before I could answer...

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:56.430
...due to circumstances beyond 
our control, he left for America.

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:56.140
And since then?

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:57.870
Since then?

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:00.120
Haven't you had any contact with him since then?

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:02.830
For example, mail or an overseas phone call?

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:05.620
Well... I have no idea how 
to get in touch with him.

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:06.330
I see...

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:07.150
But...

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:08.880
If I accomplish my dream of becoming a singer...

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:11.720
...my name might even reach 
somewhere as far as America.

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:13.050
Then surely...

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:16.760
...surely... Eichi-kun will... notice me.

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:19.430
You put your whole heart into this, huh?

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:21.060
Somewhat, I guess.

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:26.850
What is it, Takuto?

00:06:26.850 --> 00:06:28.230
You're making such a frightening face.

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:29.230
Scary...

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:31.050
What are you?

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:34.190
I thought you had honest 
feelings of becoming a singer...

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:35.740
...but it was all for a guy!

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:36.700
Eh?

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:37.970
That's just wrong!

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:40.620
If you don't have pure intentions 
of becoming a singer...

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:41.970
...you can't become a good singer!

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:42.990
You...

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:44.450
...quit singing immediately!

00:06:44.450 --> 00:06:46.460
W-Why are you saying something like that?

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:47.420
That's right.

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:48.920
Isn't it great that she's doing it because of a guy?

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:49.670
Not at all!

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:50.710
Huh?

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:52.880
I'll... work really hard at singing, so...

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:56.880
No matter how hard you work, in the back 
of your mind, you'll always feel like quitting.

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:57.760
That can't be...

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:00.930
I would never want to quit singing.

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:03.060
That's right! What part of this is immoral?!

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:05.810
What part of doing it for a guy is anyways?!

00:07:05.810 --> 00:07:07.190
Besides...

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:10.190
...such blind faith after being neglected 
 for two years is anything but normal!

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:12.320
You've been dumped.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:16.340
He's probably already with another girl over there.

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:18.280
E-Eichi-kun...

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:19.780
...would never do something like that!

00:07:19.780 --> 00:07:21.440
Why can't you understand that?

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:23.810
That's because... it's Eichi-kun, after all!

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:25.580
That's foolish.

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:26.290
Hey!

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:28.040
Cut it out, Takuto!

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:29.080
Anyways...

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:31.000
...someone as disrespectful of singing as you...

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:32.520
...will never sing again!

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:32.920
Hmph!

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:35.630
W-Wait... Takuto.

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:36.720
Takuto!

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:38.550
Come on, Takuto!

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:41.800
Geez... why is he so mad?

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:42.760
More importantly...

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:46.390
...what kind of person gets in the way of fate...

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:50.650
Someone who gets in the way of a human's fate...

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.610
...may be in love with that human.

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:56.480
This Eichi...

00:07:56.480 --> 00:07:57.570
...I'll have to pay special attention to him.

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:14.170
Just what were you thinking?

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:17.170
When I told you that you shouldn't audition...

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:19.510
...I wasn't trying to be mean.

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:22.090
It's impossible because your condition right now.

00:08:22.090 --> 00:08:23.140
Stop it.

00:08:23.430 --> 00:08:24.720
Sorry...

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:26.510
But...

00:08:26.510 --> 00:08:28.040
...it's over with now, right?

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:28.600
Eh?

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:32.060
You'll be unable to sing for a while...

00:08:32.060 --> 00:08:34.360
Ah... no, I made it.

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:35.110
Made it?

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:47.080
Hmm?

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:48.410
What do you mean by "made it"?

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:52.290
It couldn't be that... you passed the audition?

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:53.790
Um... well...

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.680
Um... I meant modeling.

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:01.780
Oh... modeling, huh?

00:09:02.090 --> 00:09:03.800
Well, modeling is fine, I suppose.

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:05.760
But from now on, don't do anything rash like this.

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:06.720
O-Okay!

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:07.850
By the way...

00:09:07.850 --> 00:09:09.390
...what'd you do for the application?

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:10.810
Under <i>guardian</i>...

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:12.640
...did you write your grandmother's name?

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:15.110
Um... actually...

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:17.780
Did you put my name down?

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:19.480
F-Forgive me!

00:09:21.020 --> 00:09:22.130
It's fine, it's fine.

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:24.140
We'll keep it a secret from your grandmother, okay?

00:09:24.820 --> 00:09:26.410
I-Is that okay?

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:27.370
Sure.

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:30.080
I understand your feelings, after all.

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:32.590
It's for Eichi-kun, right?

00:09:32.870 --> 00:09:34.190
Y-Yep!

00:09:44.030 --> 00:09:46.680
You are not allowed to leave the house.

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:48.300
Leaving the house...

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:50.840
...and having the Doctor take 
you to the amusement park...

00:09:50.840 --> 00:09:52.810
...you should be ashamed!

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:00.320
Do you understand?

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:02.470
I'm very sorry.

00:10:02.780 --> 00:10:04.010
Next time...

00:10:04.010 --> 00:10:05.700
...a simple apology will not suffice.

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:06.490
Yes.

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:09.300
That's enough.

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:10.880
Please excuse yourself.

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:11.750
Yes.

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:15.060
Hmm...

00:10:16.540 --> 00:10:17.460
Wait a minute.

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:19.200
What is that?

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:23.090
What is it?

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:24.970
T-This is...

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:26.780
Um... um...

00:10:26.780 --> 00:10:28.050
...from the crane game.

00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:31.850
Is that so?

00:10:34.430 --> 00:10:36.360
E-Excuse me.

00:10:39.880 --> 00:10:41.480
Such an annoying grandmother...

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:43.760
She kept going on and on...

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:44.850
But this means that...

00:10:44.850 --> 00:10:47.780
...you're one step closer to your dream, right?

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:48.320
Yeah.

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:48.910
Hey...

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:51.740
What kind of guy is Eichi-kun?

00:10:51.740 --> 00:10:52.830
Okay? Okay?

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:53.740
Eh...

00:10:54.020 --> 00:10:55.000
Okay.

00:10:57.250 --> 00:10:58.370
Wow!

00:10:58.370 --> 00:11:00.290
He's a pretty good-looking guy.

00:11:00.290 --> 00:11:00.750
How old is he?

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:02.710
We're six years apart, so...

00:11:02.710 --> 00:11:03.890
...right now he's eighteen.

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:08.660
So this is a picture of Eichi-kun when he was sixteen?

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:10.640
Sooo cute.

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:25.650
Eichi-kun...

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:29.280
Eichi-kun couldn't possibly...

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:54.540
So this is where you've been, huh?

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:56.050
Leave me alone.

00:11:56.050 --> 00:11:59.200
Well, that means I have nowhere left to go.

00:11:59.200 --> 00:11:59.760
Huh?

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:02.860
That girl looks like she wants to be alone, too.

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:05.150
You upset her...

00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:07.490
Eichi-kun...

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:10.690
It's all you fault, you know.

00:12:11.030 --> 00:12:11.740
Huh?

00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:15.200
She's upset because you told her she'd been dumped.

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:17.390
Well, that's what I think would have happened by now.

00:12:17.390 --> 00:12:18.430
Am I wrong?

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:20.130
Besides...

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:24.710
...constantly thinking about a guy who's already
dumped you is strange in this day and age!

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:26.420
It's <i>strange,</i> indeed.

00:12:26.420 --> 00:12:27.490
Right?

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:29.950
Always avoiding the truth...

00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:32.470
...you haven't changed at all, Takuto.

00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:34.850
Do you like her?

00:12:35.220 --> 00:12:36.400
S-Stupid.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:37.520
It's nothing like that!

00:12:37.830 --> 00:12:40.140
I-Isn't this our duty?

00:12:40.140 --> 00:12:42.020
Besides, even if I said she was dumped...

00:12:42.020 --> 00:12:46.330
I was just saying that as a general 
observation... I didn't state it very well.

00:12:46.330 --> 00:12:47.780
Such a matter...

00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:57.290
Here you go!

00:12:57.490 --> 00:12:58.160
Fortune telling?

00:12:58.160 --> 00:12:58.940
Yep.

00:12:58.940 --> 00:13:00.720
I'll read your fortune for today.

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:02.120
Pick a card.

00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:02.750
Okay.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:11.720
Which one is it?

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:13.650
Wow! That's great!

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:15.440
Today's your lucky day.

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:16.720
That's lucky?

00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:18.470
Yep. Super Lucky.

00:13:18.470 --> 00:13:19.640
The lucky word today is... shopping.

00:13:19.640 --> 00:13:20.680
The lucky word today is... shopping!

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:22.810
Something good will definitely happen.

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:24.270
Come on, let's go out.

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:24.650
Okay.

00:13:25.440 --> 00:13:27.920
Grandma's out today, too.

00:13:27.920 --> 00:13:30.610
Ah, but if I don't ask Tanaka-san...

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:43.920
Do you need something, Mitsuki-chan?

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:45.080
Um...

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:47.600
I want to go out shopping...

00:13:47.600 --> 00:13:49.880
But madam said that...

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:53.800
If Grandma learns that you listen to forbidden music...

00:13:54.130 --> 00:13:55.840
...I wonder what she'll say?

00:13:56.890 --> 00:13:58.850
You might get scolded...

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:02.310
Shall we head out?

00:14:08.440 --> 00:14:09.520
Where are they going?

00:14:12.570 --> 00:14:15.290
If Meroko's going along, then I'll 
just leave everything up to her.

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:32.710
Mitsuki-chan.

00:14:32.710 --> 00:14:37.380
Can you wait here for a little bit, please?

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:39.100
Sure, I understand.

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:42.770
Then... then... just wait a little, please!

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:43.520
Later!

00:14:44.930 --> 00:14:46.040
Hey, hey.

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:47.060
Hmm?

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:49.440
There's somewhere I want to go, too...

00:14:51.520 --> 00:14:53.740
Ah... I'm going to use the toilet, so...

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:54.780
...just wait for me outside.

00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:55.360
I got it.

00:14:59.520 --> 00:15:02.580
Shinigami have to use the restroom too, huh?

00:15:03.930 --> 00:15:05.290
She left, right?

00:15:08.580 --> 00:15:12.050
That girl listened to my suggestion to go out so readily, huh?

00:15:16.630 --> 00:15:18.970
Mero-Mero Change!

00:15:36.650 --> 00:15:37.530
It's mine!

00:15:37.530 --> 00:15:38.650
It's mine, I tell you!

00:15:46.200 --> 00:15:47.330
That good thing...

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:48.410
...I wonder what it is.

00:15:58.800 --> 00:15:59.880
That guy is...

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:06.310
It's been a long time, Mitsuki-chan.

00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:07.490
E-

00:16:08.010 --> 00:16:09.140
Eichi-kun?

00:16:11.230 --> 00:16:12.230
That guy is...?

00:16:12.430 --> 00:16:13.610
T-This can't be real.

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:15.190
It's real, all right.

00:16:28.290 --> 00:16:30.040
I'm dreaming, aren't I?

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:31.790
You're not dreaming.

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:36.130
Even though I went to America...

00:16:36.130 --> 00:16:38.920
...I never forgot about you, Mitsuki-chan.

00:16:39.510 --> 00:16:40.130
That's why...

00:16:40.130 --> 00:16:42.260
...once I heard you'd become a singer...

00:16:42.260 --> 00:16:43.970
...I hurried back to Japan.

00:16:43.970 --> 00:16:44.600
Eh?

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:45.640
My becoming a singer...

00:16:45.640 --> 00:16:46.970
...who did you hear that from?

00:16:47.600 --> 00:16:48.680
Who did I hear that from?

00:16:48.680 --> 00:16:51.350
S-Someone I know in the record business.

00:16:51.350 --> 00:16:52.100
That's how I...

00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:53.540
That's an amazing coincidence.

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:54.860
It was more than a coincidence...

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:57.400
...it was fate.

00:16:57.990 --> 00:16:59.050
Fate...

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:00.900
By the way, Eichi-kun...

00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:02.710
...what's with that voice?

00:17:02.710 --> 00:17:04.490
After going to America...

00:17:04.490 --> 00:17:06.370
...I suppose that my voice probably changed like so.

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:08.370
America's so vast... right?

00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:11.870
You're so funny.

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:12.870
R-Really?

00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:17.960
W-What is it this time?

00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:20.980
There's something I have to 
apologize to you for, Eichi-kun.

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:23.920
I... I sang... for your sake...

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:27.850
...I thought that you might have forgotten about me.

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:30.060
What? It's for that?

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:34.810
Mitsuki-chan...

00:17:35.190 --> 00:17:38.170
Will you still... like me?

00:17:38.170 --> 00:17:40.510
O-Of course.

00:17:40.510 --> 00:17:42.000
I'm so glad.

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:44.350
Back then... I...

00:17:44.350 --> 00:17:46.240
I couldn't properly answer, so...

00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:53.620
Now... I also... about you...

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:56.960
L-

00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:02.090
I'm... I'm... I'm sorry!

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:03.880
Where are you going?

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:04.510
Ah.

00:18:05.790 --> 00:18:07.490
Shinigami-san.

00:18:07.490 --> 00:18:09.010
That isn't Eichi.

00:18:09.010 --> 00:18:09.890
It's Meroko.

00:18:09.890 --> 00:18:10.600
Eh?

00:18:11.020 --> 00:18:11.790
You're kidding.

00:18:12.380 --> 00:18:13.330
I'm not kidding.

00:18:13.890 --> 00:18:16.820
We Shinigami are capable of transformation.

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:19.360
Is... that so..?

00:18:21.730 --> 00:18:22.650
That's right.

00:18:23.780 --> 00:18:26.780
Eichi-kun... has no reason to be here, right?

00:18:26.780 --> 00:18:28.670
I've made you wait!

00:18:29.490 --> 00:18:31.080
Is something wrong, Mitsuki-chan?

00:18:31.490 --> 00:18:32.200
No.

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:33.450
There's nothing wrong.

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:35.410
Your face looks pale.

00:18:35.790 --> 00:18:37.420
Come, let's go home.

00:18:43.800 --> 00:18:45.170
That was low!

00:18:45.170 --> 00:18:46.930
You've really done it now!

00:18:47.400 --> 00:18:50.260
I thought it was a good idea...

00:18:50.260 --> 00:18:51.920
How was that a good idea?!

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:53.750
Someone's serious matter...

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:55.480
...a person's pure feelings...

00:18:55.480 --> 00:18:57.480
...you were just toying with them!

00:18:57.480 --> 00:18:58.980
I'm sorry...

00:18:58.980 --> 00:19:00.460
You think that apologizing will solve this?

00:19:00.460 --> 00:19:01.000
Wait.

00:19:01.270 --> 00:19:01.730
Huh?

00:19:01.730 --> 00:19:05.440
Pure... didn't you just say that they were immoral?

00:19:05.440 --> 00:19:06.080
Huh?

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:06.880
I said that?

00:19:06.880 --> 00:19:08.110
You sure did!

00:19:08.110 --> 00:19:10.710
"What part of doing it for a guy
is moral?", something like that.

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:11.160
That...

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:14.000
That was about becoming a singer...

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:16.410
That and this are two totally unrelated matters!

00:19:16.410 --> 00:19:17.410
Really?

00:19:17.750 --> 00:19:20.420
I guess that I was pretty cruel...

00:19:20.420 --> 00:19:22.960
But all that stuff about Eichi...

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:24.210
...being dumped and all...

00:19:24.210 --> 00:19:25.720
What are you going to do about it, Takuto?

00:19:27.260 --> 00:19:30.450
Don't you think that your words hurt her?

00:19:41.900 --> 00:19:42.900
Um...

00:19:43.230 --> 00:19:46.150
What I said about you being dumped 
just me being a devil's advocate...

00:19:46.150 --> 00:19:46.940
...I didn't mean it.

00:19:47.260 --> 00:19:48.860
It's just a possibility.

00:19:49.240 --> 00:19:50.600
No... that's...

00:19:51.320 --> 00:19:51.950
I'm sorry.

00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:52.980
No.

00:19:52.980 --> 00:19:54.440
I was also at fault.

00:19:55.810 --> 00:19:58.890
If I really believed in Eichi-kun...

00:19:58.890 --> 00:20:01.500
...no matter what was said... I wouldn't be worried.

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:03.540
That's why I won't be confused anymore.

00:20:04.710 --> 00:20:06.920
I... I love Eichi-kun!

00:20:07.800 --> 00:20:09.300
But, just as much as that...

00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:10.180
...I love singing!

00:20:10.970 --> 00:20:11.840
If I love him...

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:13.680
...then I have to believe in him!

00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:15.390
I have to do my best to believe in him!

00:20:15.390 --> 00:20:17.890
If I don't, then my dream will never come true!

00:20:18.140 --> 00:20:18.980
These feelings...

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:21.020
...will never be impure!

00:20:23.770 --> 00:20:25.070
I guess it can't be helped.

00:20:25.600 --> 00:20:27.580
Do whatever you want to do.

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:28.520
For the next year...

00:20:28.520 --> 00:20:30.650
...I'll work to fulfill your dream.

00:20:30.650 --> 00:20:32.000
You will?

00:20:32.990 --> 00:20:33.740
My blood will...

00:20:33.740 --> 00:20:35.990
...always be inside you, so...

00:20:35.990 --> 00:20:37.830
...I'll always be able to transform you.

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:40.720
When I'm not with you...

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:43.630
...use this whistle to call me.

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:44.720
I'll fly to you.

00:20:45.670 --> 00:20:47.880
Thank you, Shinigami-san!

00:20:48.080 --> 00:20:49.800
Stop it with the "Shinigami-san".

00:20:49.800 --> 00:20:50.840
Call me Takuto.

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:51.530
Okay.

00:20:51.530 --> 00:20:53.260
Thank you, Takuto.

00:20:53.260 --> 00:20:54.000
Anytime.

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:55.250
Could it be that...

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:57.200
...I've become the evil villain?

00:20:59.020 --> 00:20:59.430
Ah.

00:20:59.430 --> 00:21:00.540
Usagi-san!

00:21:01.060 --> 00:21:04.020
I wanted to thank you.

00:21:04.020 --> 00:21:05.150
T-Thank me?

00:21:05.150 --> 00:21:05.940
Yep.

00:21:05.940 --> 00:21:08.940
Because today really was my lucky day!

00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:11.450
You changed into Eichi-kun...

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:13.850
...to give me courage, right?

00:21:14.380 --> 00:21:16.410
I'm really sorry!

00:21:17.650 --> 00:21:18.240
Eh?

00:21:18.240 --> 00:21:20.050
Why is Usagi-san apologizing?

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:21.370
Who knows?

00:21:21.370 --> 00:21:22.690
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:21:22.690 --> 00:21:23.760
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:25.540
I'll never do it again!

00:23:06.390 --> 00:23:07.310
Takuto!

00:23:07.310 --> 00:23:08.350
There's an emergency... an emergency!

00:23:08.350 --> 00:23:11.070
Her manager is coming to meet her!

00:23:11.070 --> 00:23:12.220
You can't mean that...

00:23:12.220 --> 00:23:13.150
That's right!

00:23:13.150 --> 00:23:14.360
Mitsuki's guardian...

00:23:14.360 --> 00:23:16.840
...Dr. Wakaouji is going to find out.

00:23:16.840 --> 00:23:17.740
Wait...

00:23:17.740 --> 00:23:20.430
That person won't recognize her when she's twelve...

00:23:20.430 --> 00:23:23.660
She came to meet her as a sixteen year old, right?

00:23:23.660 --> 00:23:25.330
What are we gonna do, Takuto?!

00:23:25.330 --> 00:23:27.000
Ahhhhh... I don't know anymore!

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:28.700
Whatever happens, happens!

00:23:28.700 --> 00:23:30.420
Next Time on Full Moon wo Sagashite:

00:23:30.420 --> 00:23:32.040
Along Came the Manager.

00:23:30.420 --> 00:23:32.040
Along Came the Manager.
